  <prompt>
    Add unit tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` covering the CIAM external-access surface: CIAM scheme token validation, provisioner idempotency, oid Contact resolution, grant-without-synthetic-SPE, and download authz-before-stream (POSITIVE and NEGATIVE — unauthorized → 403, no bytes, no Graph call). Follow ADR-038: integration-heavy; NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, NO DI-registration or ctor-null-check tests.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    You are a BFF test engineer writing behavior-focused tests against the Phase-2 CIAM surface contracts, adhering to the ADR-038 integration-heavy pyramid and mock-boundary bans.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` exist and pass covering: (1) CIAM scheme token validation (valid authenticates / invalid-issuer 401), (2) provisioner idempotency (oid-present → no second account), (3) oid Contact resolution (oid match; email mismatch denied when oid bound), (4) grant-without-synthetic-SPE (access record + invalidation, no synthetic write), and (5) download authz-before-stream POSITIVE (authorized → bytes) and NEGATIVE (unauthorized → 403, no bytes, no Graph call); no banned test shapes are introduced.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      §10 bullet 6 + NFR-07 require tests for modifications to `Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/` and `Api/ExternalAccess/`. The most consequential is the download authz-before-stream negative case (NFR-03): an unauthorized caller must receive 403 with no bytes and no Graph call. Tests must follow ADR-038: integration-heavy, KEEP-path categories only; the bans on `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration tests, and ctor-null-check tests apply. This task is TEST-MODIFYING, so code-review + adr-check run unconditionally at Step 9.5.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/InviteExternalUserEndpoint.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/ExternalCallerAuthorizationFilter.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: all tests authored here. Integration-heavy pyramid; use the KEEP-path categories. MUST NOT use `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, MUST NOT write DI-registration tests, MUST NOT write ctor null-check tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project-NFR-03">Scope: the download tests. MUST include the authz-before-stream NEGATIVE case asserting an unauthorized caller gets 403, receives NO bytes, and triggers NO Graph content read.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec-FR-08">Scope: the provisioner test. MUST assert idempotency — an already-provisioned Contact (oid present) does not create a second CIAM account.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: this BFF/test task. Tests live in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` per §10 bullet 6; the wrap-up PR references them. (No new runtime surface added — publish-size unchanged; note it.)</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read `.claude/constraints/testing.md` + `docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md` for the KEEP-path categories and mock-boundary bans; inspect existing `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` external-access tests for fixture conventions.</step>
    <step>Add CIAM scheme validation tests: a valid CIAM token authenticates on `/api/v1/external/*`; an invalid-issuer token returns 401.</step>
    <step>Add provisioner idempotency tests: first invite creates an account + persists oid; re-invite for an oid-present Contact creates no second account.</step>
    <step>Add oid-resolution tests: oid match resolves the Contact; when an oid is bound, an email mismatch does not grant access.</step>
    <step>Add grant tests: `/grant` creates `sprk_externalrecordaccess` + invalidates cache and writes NO synthetic `contact_{guid}` SPE permission.</step>
    <step>Add download authz-before-stream tests: authorized → bytes; unauthorized → 403 with no bytes and no Graph content read asserted.</step>
    <step>Run `dotnet test` for the affected project and confirm all added tests pass.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output>Unit tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` covering the five listed areas.</output>
    <output>Passing `dotnet test` run for the affected test project.</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A test asserts a valid CIAM token authenticates and an invalid-issuer token returns 401.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test asserts provisioner idempotency (oid-present → no second CIAM account).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test asserts oid resolution: oid match resolves; email mismatch denied when oid bound.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test asserts `/grant` creates the access record + invalidates cache and writes no synthetic SPE permission.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test asserts download POSITIVE (authorized → bytes) AND the NEGATIVE case asserts unauthorized → 403 with NO bytes returned and NO Graph call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no test uses `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null-check shapes (ADR-038 bans).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All added tests pass under `dotnet test`.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

